 "style": {
  "name": "Triumphal Arch, teal-orange-yellow-cream",
  "rationale": "Second pass. Mismatches found in pass one: (1) the arch read as a pointed parabola, so I rebuilt it as a true semicircle (radius 8, springing y24, crown y32) cut by exclusion row by row; (2) the voussoir ring was a thin stair-step, so it is now two stacked 1-block rings (outer at +1, inner at +2) with a projecting keystone at +3 and a coffered soffit of alternating teal and orange courses; (3) the sculpture groups were arrow-shaped slivers, so each is now a three-figure cluster (warrior, central standard-bearer, kneeling figure) on an orange relief backdrop with heads at +3, standing on a cream pedestal ledge with an orange moulding; (4) the panels lacked depth, so each is a teal frame at +1 around a recessed teal field (-1) with raised orange figures at 0; (5) the entablature and attic were mushy, so the entablature is now architrave +1, recessed teal frieze with gold and orange inscription and gold plaque, alternating dentils, and a +4 cornice with upside-down acacia stairs, and the attic is a yellow recessed panel (-1) with teal pilasters, gold rosettes, orange base band and +3 cornice; (6) the crown is 1-wide teal merlons with a low orange centre strip. Palette placement: cream cut and smooth sandstone piers with a faint chiseled checker base, yellow upper storey, teal plinth, frieze band, ring, frames, pilasters and merlons, orange impost, cornices, dentils and keystone, gold only for rosettes and the plaque. The whole facade is one connected slab 5 deep (z4-8), and all recesses are carved by omitting front material."
 },
